  },
  {
   "id": "b11-text-65",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 18,
   "y": 999,
   "width": 1590,
   "height": 43,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 514735,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 6807385,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A PQ node is a router S can reach without the failed link that also reaches E without it. S tunnels to the cheapest one (lowest cost from S, then lowest id), going out\nthrough the exit neighbor if it is only in extended P-space. In Example 4 that is PE2, through P2.",
   "originalText": "A PQ node is a router S can reach without the failed link that also reaches E without it. S tunnels to the cheapest one (lowest cost from S, then lowest id), going out\nthrough the exit neighbor if it is only in extended P-space. In Example 4 that is PE2, through P2.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "b11-text-66",
   "type": "text",
